    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## What changed\n\nDuplicate detection previously ran as **three independent checks** in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (telephone, then email, then household), each with its own exception and 409 handler. I consolidated all of it into a **single derived `identityKey`**.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + (householdId or empty)`**, added as a derived getter on the `Owner` domain object \u2014 the natural home for the key's format:\n\n```java\npublic String getIdentityKey() {\n    return String.join(\"|\",\n        this.telephone == null ? \"\" : this.telephone,\n        this.email == null ? \"\" : this.email,\n        this.householdId == null ? \"\" : this.householdId);\n}\n```\n\n### Files touched\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getIdentityKey()`. Because telephone is part of the key, two household members (same `householdId`) with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match collides.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema, so it's returned in responses (auto-wired into `OwnerDto` and MapStruct by name, exactly like the other derived fields).\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 new `isDuplicateIdentity(Owner)`. It narrows by telephone via the existing `findByTelephone` (owners with a different telephone can't share the key), then confirms the whole key matches \u2014 reusing existing repository code rather than a full scan.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 replaced the three checks with one identity-key check. Household-join still runs first (when `sharesHousehold`) so the assigned `householdId` is part of the key before the check.\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException`** (new) replaces `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateEmailException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException` (deleted).\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 the three 409 handlers collapse into one `handleDuplicateIdentityException` returning 409 with `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nThe separate telephone-only, email-only, and household-only rejections are gone. A new owner is rejected with **409 only when its whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's**.\n\n### Tests\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and I confirmed the generated `OwnerDto` and mapper actually carry `identityKey` through to the response.",
